    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "solution": "<p style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Sol: Correct Answer:&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">liberty</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">Explanation:</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">The underlined word \"yoke\" refers to oppression or bondage, making \"liberty\" the best antonym as it signifies freedom from such constraints.</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Other antonyms Words:</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">freedom, independence, emancipation, autonomy, liberation</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Let's see the meaning of all the words along with their usage:</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">yoke</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">&nbsp;– </span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">जुए (</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">jue) – A symbol of oppression or servitude.</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Example: \"The peasants struggled under the yoke of feudalism.\"</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">alacrity</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">&nbsp;– </span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">तत्परता (</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">tatparata) – Cheerful readiness or eagerness.</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Example: \"She accepted the invitation with alacrity.\"</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">fraternity</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">&nbsp;– </span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">भाईचारा (</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">bhaichara) – Brotherhood or a group of people sharing </span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">common interests.</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Example: \"The college fraternity organized a charity event.\"</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">mediocrity</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">&nbsp;– </span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">सामान्यता (</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">samanyata) – The quality of being average or ordinary.</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Example: \"He refused to settle for mediocrity and aimed for excellence.\"</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">liberty</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">&nbsp;– </span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">स्वतंत्रता (</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">svatantrata) – The state of being free from oppressive restrictions.</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">Example: \"After years of struggle, the nation finally achieved liberty.\"</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000; font-weight: bold;\">Conclusion:</span><br><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 13.5pt; color: #000000;\">\"Liberty\" is the most appropriate antonym of \"yoke\" because it directly opposes the idea of oppression and represents freedom. The other options do not convey the opposite meaning of bondage.</span></p>",
    "marks": "2",
